In order to turn the command line output of MOPSA into a `html` file, the
`ansi2html` command line tool can be used.

It is enough to pipe the output of MOPSA to `ansi2html` to generate some html
output. As a post-processing (done by hand, but as a future improvement this
could be automated) the header and the `<body>` tags shall be removed, and the
main part shall be wrapped in a `<div class="highlight">` tag.

See also the other `*.out.html` files as a reference on how the output should
look like.
